cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Enterprise World Model Engine in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Enterprise World Model Engine: An Open Framework for Modeling, Simulating, and Evaluating Organizational Dynamics"
abstract: "Enterprise World Model Engine (EWM Engine) is an open-source, domain-neutral Python framework for modeling, simulating, and evaluating complex organizational and socio-technical systems under interventional policy changes. Unlike observational predictive models, EWM executes action-conditioned forward rollouts that strictly decouple known explicit rules and conservation laws from learned probabilistic dynamics — guaranteeing deterministic reproducibility under pinned runtimes through cryptographic state fingerprints, seed-tree isolation, a three-tier backend reproducibility contract (BITWISE_REPRODUCIBLE, NUMERICALLY_EQUIVALENT_WITH_TOLERANCE, NON_CERTIFIED_BACKEND), and zero mandatory LLM dependencies."
